2026-10-13T16:22:03.2420946Z route groups to ANY admin-permissioned token, including one whose only membership is an
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2421589Z admin seat in a single workspace:
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2422073Z   1. POST|GET /v1/admin/self-update, POST /v1/admin/rollback, POST|GET /v1/admin/site-deploy
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2422487Z   2. GET /v1/plugins
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2422809Z   3. GET|PUT|DELETE /v1/plugins/settings/:plugin_name
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2423241Z   4. GET /v1/secrets, GET /v1/secrets/:name, GET /v1/secrets/:name/audit,
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2423681Z      PUT /v1/secrets/:name, DELETE /v1/secrets/:name
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2424077Z   5. POST /v1/status/incidents, POST /v1/status/incidents/:id/resolve
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2424530Z   6. POST /api/playground
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2424838Z   7. POST /api/workspaces/:workspace_slug/import
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2425209Z   8. GET /v1/instance/site-deploy, GET /v1/instance/metrics
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2426016Z On a SINGLE-TENANT instance that is fine — the only admin is the operator. On a
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2426621Z MULTI-TENANT one it hands your first customer-admin the instance: run-secrets in
2026-10-13T16:22:03.2427117Z cleartext, the instance-wide plugin credentials record, and the release itself.
